// What rib_event answers while a menu is open, from the widget's bits rbi_b for an event of kind rbi_kind, rbi_on being 1 when a press was on the control that opened the menu: 8 says the menu took the event, 1 is kept, a choice is 11, and a press outside is 9 when it was on the opener (the press closes the menu and no more) or 5 elsewhere (the menu is closed and the press is not used up).
ribbon_popup_answer(int ribbon_popup_answer_bits, int ribbon_popup_answer_kind, int ribbon_popup_answer_on_opener) {
  int ribbon_popup_answer_result = (ribbon_popup_answer_bits & 1) + 8;
  if((ribbon_popup_answer_bits & 2) != 0) {
    ribbon_popup_answer_result = 11;
  }
  if((ribbon_popup_answer_bits & 4) != 0) {
    ribbon_popup_answer_result = 9 - 4 * (ribbon_popup_answer_kind == 3) * (ribbon_popup_answer_on_opener == 0);
  }
} return int ribbon_popup_answer_result;
(2, 4, 0):(11)
(4, 3, 0):(5)
(4, 3, 1):(9)
(4, 1, 0):(9)
(0, 5, 0):(8)

